      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Broadmoor’s historic district, listed on the National Register of Historic Places in 2003, contains nearly 800 historic structures.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://prcno.org/help-for-homeowners/historic-districts-neighborhoods/broadmoor/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Rosa Keller Library branch, with a historic brick façade and Spanish tile roof, now sports an ultra‑modern addition that showcases the neighborhood’s architectural diversity.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://prcno.org/help-for-homeowners/historic-districts-neighborhoods/broadmoor/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Development in Broadmoor began in the 1880s when the marshy pasture flooded after heavy rains, creating a lake that attracted Uptown fishermen.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11,
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://prcno.org/help-for-homeowners/historic-districts-neighborhoods/broadmoor/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "The Broadmoor Civic Improvement Association, formed in the 1880s, was one of New Orleans’ first neighborhood associations.",
